        "market_heading": "Why home staging matters in the Tampa market",
        "market_text": "<p>Tampa Bay has spent years near the top of national relocation lists, and the buyers arriving from the Northeast and Midwest do most of their shopping before the moving truck is booked. For them the listing photos are the property tour — and an empty stucco ranch with tile floors reads as an echo, not a home.</p><p>The bay itself does heavy lifting in local marketing: staged waterfront lanais, pool decks and bonus rooms consistently out-perform interior shots. Our home staging covers outdoor living too, and day-to-dusk editing turns a flat exterior into the sunset-over-the-water shot.</p><p>Tampa's inventory also skews toward the two hardest room types to photograph empty: wide-open great rooms in newer builds, where there's nothing to establish scale, and tiled Florida rooms that read as unfinished space until furniture gives them a purpose.</p>",
